  "notes": "Xiaomi MiTV-ASTP0 (codename mulan; China-market firmware, sold as L55M7-EA), Android 9 (SDK 28),\nfirmware 22.12.2.1630, Amlogic/droidlogic, 1.5 GB RAM, 1080p panel. Used in Vietnam.\nStock launcher: com.mitv.tvhome (HOME activity .MainActivityUserMode). It is not in\nKNOWN_STOCK_LAUNCHERS, so install with: STOCK_LAUNCHER=com.mitv.tvhome launcher/build-and-install.sh\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-astp0/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/xiaomi-mitv-astp0/debloat.txt com.mitv.tvhome\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- Same family as xiaomi-mitv-astp1; this list starts from that one, minus what this build lacks\n(com.gitvdemo.video, com.duokan.videodaily, com.xiaomi.tv.gallery, com.newtv.cboxtv).\n- No CN streaming apps preinstalled; no Google apps besides the YouTube and katniss the owner sideloaded.\n- Network ADB (port 5555) closes on every reboot; re-enable it in\nSettings -> Account & Security -> ADB debugging after each power cycle. Wi-Fi also sleeps in\nstandby, so the TV drops off the network until it is woken.\n- mitv.service is the core MiTV service: do not touch it. The owner chose to drop payment, Mi Home,\nMi Video, the voice assistant and every casting receiver but AirPlay (in com.xiaomi.mitv.smartshare).\nThe app store and com.mitv.videoplayer (USB files) stay.\n- com.xiaomi.mitv.remotecontroller.service looped at 100-190% CPU and flooded logd (~490 MB in\n30 min): its relay host is gone, so it is disabled below. ES File Explorer ran DLNA and a WebView\nin the background; it is replaced by Material Files (F-Droid, me.zhanghai.android.files).\n- Home stays com.mitv.tvhome: set-home-activity succeeds but resolution ignores it, and with\ncom.mitv.tvhome disabled Home falls to com.android.tv.settings/.system.FallbackHome. Keep it\nenabled; an accessibility service that answers the Home key (HOME_KEY_SERVICE=1) brings the new\nlauncher up instead.\n- The firmware has no night mode setting: cmd uimode night yes|no|auto. Auto needs a location for\nsunset and the TV has none, so it stays in day mode.\n- The remote has no Input button; its Menu key (three lines) is KEYCODE_MENU, scancode 127. Inputs\nswitch only through Xiaomi's player: am start -a com.xiaomi.mitv.tvplayer.EXTSRC_PLAY\n-n com.xiaomi.mitv.tvplayer/.ExternalSourceActivity --ei input N (HDMI1-3 = 23-25, AV = 2).\nStarting the HDMI channel URI with a plain VIEW lets any app that claims every VIEW catch it.\n- The time zone ships as Asia/Shanghai, an hour ahead in Vietnam. Set the one the IP locates\n(get.geojs.io/v1/ip/geo.json \"timezone\"): service call alarm 3 s16 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n- Picture: Settings -> Image settings -> Display model is kept per source; \"Picture\" is the vivid\none (contrast 55, saturation 60, cold), \"Standard\" is flat.\nXiaomi telemetry / push / cloud control",
